WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.180
Then I jumped in my rental car, called my
mom, and then crashed into you.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.440
Thank God.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.280
"That's not your dad in the picture.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.170
I did buy ecstasy from him, though.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.450
Yum." She sounds fun.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.620
She is.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.630
Oh, God, that's so great.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.920
He's not my dad.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.440
It's just another great guy that I ran away
from because I'm a complete mess.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:30.760
Who?

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.410
When you were little, who did you picture
when you were imagining him?

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.430
Bryan Cranston from Malcolm in the Middle.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.050
Not Breaking Bad.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.110
I couldn't even watch that. I didn't want to
see my dad cooking meth.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.770
For me, it was Bob Barker.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.660
I always dreamed that one day he'd pull up
outside my school and we'd go spay and neuter

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.530
pets together.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:57.940
Yeah.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.390
So you don't know your dad either?

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.890
Actually, now I do.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:09.010
A great friend of mine lost his father a
while back, and so I decided to track down my

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.480
own before it was too late.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.960
Did you ever think about finding yours?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:22.090
Of course. But then I worry that he's going
to be a criminal or a drunk or a prop comic.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:22.660
Eww.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.380
And then other times I think that he would be
everything that's ever been missing from my

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:37.270
life and completely transform me into the
best version of myself that I could be.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.550
Fix your abandonment issues, your commitment
issues.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.190
You're not seeing women as human being
issues.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.820
Did your dad do all of that for you?

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.500
Ha, No.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.680
Actually, a few years back, a really amazing
girl came into my life.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.820
My daughter, Ellie.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:05.280
She is the best thing that ever happened to
an idiot like me.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.170
The moment I saw her, I knew I had to
change.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.590
Don't get me wrong.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.930
My dad is great.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.180
He's kind and funny.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.430
And watching the two of them together, it
just.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.510
You got it. Yeah.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.860
Look, if you ever do decide to track down
your dad.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:38.580
It probably won't fix all your problems.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.920
But if you get lucky like I did, it'd be
great.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.440
So was my story juicy enough for you, or are
you going to make me pay?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.470
You're off the hook.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.320
You don't have to venmo me anything.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.430
Or as my past self used to say, you don't
have to "VenmoHoe" me.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.970
I said past self.

